In mathematics a multiple integral is a definite integral of a function of several real variables, for instance, f(x, y) or f(x, y, z). 

Integrals of a function of two variables over a region in R² (the real-number plane) are called double integrals, and integrals of a function of three variables over a region in R³ (real-number 3D space) are called triple integrals
